Chromium 156.0.8078.47 + the later changes of its release branch, for the
156.0.8078.47 tree that chromium-156.0.8078.12-to-156.0.8078.35.patch and
chromium-156.0.8078.35-to-156.0.8078.47.patch make.

The 156 branch has gained fixes since 156.0.8078.47 (in editing, SVG
animation in <use> trees, FEDisplacementMap, the HTTP cache, headless mode,
ICU, V8, Skia's Vulkan backend and WebRTC), some of them likely security fixes
that later release notes will credit.

Generated from the upstream diffs chromium/src
refs/tags/156.0.8078.47..3cb2f75a39c46a893dfa644b3e16013a4b6135d7
(refs/branch-heads/8078 on 2026-10-20, 48 commits) and the dependencies
whose DEPS revision changed (v8, third_party/skia, third_party/webrtc,
third_party/icu), as served by Gitiles, with the same rules as
chromium-156.0.8078.12-to-156.0.8078.35.patch: left out are files not in the
release tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations other than en-GB (Chromium's .xtb files and DevTools' locale
files), PGO/AFDO/orderfile pointers, ChromeOS LKGM,
submodule pointer updates. chrome/VERSION, DEPS and the generated LASTCHANGE
files stay at 156.0.8078.47.

Commits contributing to it (oldest first; "Roll commits from side projects"
are the v8, skia and webrtc updates):
  427db60c7e26 Roll commits from side projects in M156
  4c67b46435ac [M156] [Editing] Copy id attribute when undoing a split
  cc11293118a6 Roll commits from side projects in M156
  aa562b9e07a1 [M156] HttpCache: prevent lock timeout overtaking explicit restart
  7c74a2cb07fe [M156] Disable FEDisplacementMap acting as a backdrop-filter
  ae9ac8317edd Roll commits from side projects in M156
  94bace9c2c99 [M156] Make timed elements inserted into <use> shadow trees inert
  7b0b15f0ff3e [M156] Roll src/third_party/icu/ 19dfb44a6..4fe960221 (2 commits)
  c5f3959f2501 Roll commits from side projects in M156
  15da27e569d0 [M156] [headless] Do not mutate process CommandLine in ProcessHeadlessCommands

Checked: applies to the 156.0.8078.47 tree; every patched file is
byte-identical to its version at the commits above.

